518
00:30:46.328 --> 00:30:47.096
5.

519
00:30:47.376 --> 00:30:48.571
Proposed design.

520
00:30:48.851 --> 00:31:11.549
Resilience4j in the service template with per-dependency instances configured from application.yml: timeouts from the deadline (Ch 17), breakers (count window 20 to 50, failure rate 50 %, slow-call 1 s or 50 %, open 5 s with a cap, 3 probes), semaphore bulkheads, and no retries except where explicitly allowed.

521
00:31:11.829 --> 00:31:12.896
Ingress shedding:

522
00:31:13.176 --> 00:31:27.768
Tomcat or Jetty thread and queue limits aligned with the service's concurrency, a filter that drops requests whose deadline has passed or that waited 250 ms, and 503 + Retry-After responses.

523
00:31:29.118 --> 00:31:40.318
Gateway: token-bucket rate limits per API key and per customer (Redis), priority classes (checkout browse prefetch), and a single retry for idempotent GETs with jitter.

524
00:31:40.598 --> 00:31:47.979
Shared-dependency limiters: a Redis Lua token bucket per vendor (SMS, Razorpay settlement APIs, ERP).

525
00:31:48.259 --> 00:31:55.427
Degradation catalogue: every degradable feature has an owner, a fallback, a flag and a quarterly game-day test.

