00:36:11.335 --> 00:36:34.055
100 units per 10 ms tick, serve = 1 unit, reject. = 0.25 unit. retry schedule peak calls or tick all served after total calls. immediate retry (every tick) 1000 never (100 s) 10,000,000. fixed 100 ms 1000 never (100 s) 1,000,000. exponential (10ms, 2^n,

611
00:36:34.335 --> 00:36:52.340
cap 2 s) 1000 never (100 s) 56,000. exponential + full jitter 1000 540 ms 4,327. exponential + equal jitter 1000 290 ms 4,059.

612
00:36:55.190 --> 00:37:02.315
What L1 shows: when rejecting costs capacity, synchronized retries keep the server above capacity forever.

613
00:37:02.595 --> 00:37:07.438
A fixed delay or plain exponential backoff only moves the synchronized wave.

614
00:37:07.718 --> 00:37:12.369
Jitter spreads it below capacity, and everyone is served in well under a second.

615
00:37:12.649 --> 00:37:16.147
